<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Workflow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <Workflow> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        NEW FILE, 2026-08-19. Disposition__c had no workflow metadata before this change.

        🔴 THIS FILE CONTAINS EXACTLY ONE FIELD UPDATE AND NO WORKFLOW RULE, AND THE ABSENCE OF
        A RULE IS THE POINT. Set_Approval_Advance_Pending is never fired by a criteria-based
        workflow rule. It is fired ONLY as a finalApprovalActions entry by three approval
        processes on this object:
            approvalProcesses/Disposition__c.Sale_Decision_Approval
            approvalProcesses/Disposition__c.Broker_Selection_Approval
            approvalProcesses/Disposition__c.Closing_Approval
        Do not add a <rules> element here to "activate" it - an active workflow rule writing this
        flag would fire a stage advance on an ordinary record edit.

        WHY A FIELD UPDATE ON A FLAG RATHER THAN ON Disposition_Stage__c ITSELF (design D-1):
        an approval FieldUpdate BYPASSES VALIDATION RULES ENTIRELY, so a direct stage write
        would let an approval skip the all-NDAs-signed gate and the wire gate. The flag is a
        SEMAPHORE: it re-fires DispositionTrigger, whose after-update handler detects false to
        true and enqueues DispositionApprovalAdvanceQueueable, which writes the stage with
        ordinary Database.update(..., false, AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE) - validation rules still
        evaluate, the approver's CRUD is irrelevant, and the recordEditability = AdminOnly lock
        has definitively released by the time the job runs. An approval-triggered FLOW was also
        rejected: with no runInMode it executes as the APPROVER, a measured incident on this org.
        The full reasoning lives in the XML comment on
        objects/Disposition__c/fields/Approval_Advance_Pending__c.field-meta.xml.

        ⚠ reevaluateOnChange IS false ON PURPOSE. It controls re-evaluation of WORKFLOW RULES,
        not of triggers. Triggers re-run on a field update regardless, which is exactly the
        mechanism D-1 depends on; turning this on would only add a workflow re-evaluation pass
        that has nothing to evaluate.

        ⚠ ONE UPDATE SERVES ALL THREE APPROVALS. It carries no information about WHICH approval
        set it - the Queueable derives the target from (record type, current stage). Approval
        history is where "who approved what" lives. Do not split this into three flags.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. This file must land BEFORE the three approval processes: an
        approval process referencing a field update that does not exist fails the deploy. It
        must also land WITH or AFTER Approval_Advance_Pending__c.field-meta.xml.
    -->
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>Set_Approval_Advance_Pending</fullName>
        <description>Sets the D-1 auto-advance semaphore. Fired as a final approval action by Sale Decision, Broker Selection and Closing approvals; read and cleared by DispositionApprovalAdvanceQueueable, which writes the next stage.</description>
        <field>Approval_Advance_Pending__c</field>
        <literalValue>1</literalValue>
        <name>Set Approval Advance Pending</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
</Workflow>
